From c724ad771938912eeae5b57a7bc98f90e5cadf36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M7 <m7@local>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:53:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?test(vm2):=20AVM=5FSIM=5FTESTS=20=E2=80=94=20th?=
 =?UTF-8?q?e=20simulation-side=20test=20suite,=20buildable=20for=20wasm?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`vm2_sim` is declared with no `TEST_SOURCE_FILES`, and the `vm2_tests` binary
that carries them is created inside `if(AVM)` from a recursive glob of *every*
`*.test.cpp` under `vm2/`, linked against `sumcheck stdlib_honk_verifier
goblin_avm` and, one line further down, `dsl vm2`. None of that is available in
an `AVM_WASM` build, and none of it is needed by the tests that sit beside
`vm2_sim`'s own sources.

Add `option(AVM_SIM_TESTS ... OFF)`, and under it give `vm2_sim` its own
`TEST_SOURCE_FILES` — the `simulation/`, `common/` and `tooling/` test sources,
plus the test-support translation units from `testing/` that upstream compiles
into the `vm2` module. The binary is then produced by `cmake/module.cmake`'s own
machinery: the same `add_executable`, the same gtest/gmock linkage, the same
`-Wl,-z,stack-size=8388608` under WASM and the same `gtest_discover_tests`
natively. Default OFF, so no existing configuration gains or loses a target.

Measured at `233d8e0993` + the four AVM_WASM series patches: `vm2_tests` declares
1,803 tests, `vm2_sim_tests` 391, and the 391 are a subset of the 1,803 name for
name. Native and `wasm32-wasip1` both run 391 from 60 suites and pass all of
them, with identical name sets.

Four things were needed to get there, each of them a defect on its own terms:

* `cmake/gtest.cmake`: googletest's own CMake puts `-DGTEST_HAS_PTHREAD=1` in
  `cxx_base_flags` whenever `find_package(Threads)` succeeds — which it does
  under wasi-sdk, whose sysroot carries pthread stubs — and applies it to gtest's
  four translation units only. Consumers of the headers then see the header's own
  default, which is 0 for wasi, so `internal::MutexBase` is a different type on
  the two sides of the library boundary. Every wasm test binary that mixes them
  is an ODR violation; it surfaces as `pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex_) failed with
  error 16` or as `Condition has_owner_ && pthread_equal(owner_, pthread_self())
  failed` out of gmock's global expectation registry. `GTEST_HAS_EXCEPTIONS=0`
  and `GTEST_HAS_STREAM_REDIRECTION=0` were `PRIVATE` on gtest for the same
  reason and have the same problem — and `GTEST_HAS_EXCEPTIONS=0` is simply wrong
  for an `AVM_WASM` build, which compiles with `-fwasm-exceptions`. Turn pthread
  support off on both sides and let the exceptions macro detect itself.

* `-Wl,-u,__main_argc_argv` on the wasm test binary. wasi-sdk's clang renames
  `int main(int, char**)` to `__main_argc_argv`, and wasi-libc's `__main_void`
  references it weakly, so wasm-ld never searches `libgtest_main.a`; the entry
  point resolves to an undefined-weak stub and the module traps at `unreachable`
  before the first test. Naming the symbol as required pulls gtest's own main, so
  the wasm binary runs the same program as the native one.

* Five test translation units carry 24 narrowing conversions that are only
  diagnosed where `size_t` is 32-bit: `indexed_tree_check.test.cpp` (5),
  `public_data_tree_check.test.cpp` (12), `update_check.test.cpp` (1),
  `call_stack_metadata_collector.test.cpp` (3) and `hinting_dbs.test.cpp` (3).
  Seventeen of the 24 are `MemoryTree::update_element` / `get_sibling_path`,
  which take `size_t`, called with a `uint64_t` or an `index_t`. They are made
  explicit at the call sites rather than by changing `memory_tree.hpp`'s
  signatures, which is a library API used well outside these tests.

* `testing/fixtures.cpp`: `empty_trace()` and `get_minimal_trace_with_pi()` build
  a tracegen trace, which is the proving side. They are guarded by
  `AVM_SIM_TESTS_WITHOUT_TRACEGEN`, and `common/avm_io.test.cpp` — their only
  caller among the simulation-side tests — is excluded from the target.

The 1,412 tests outside `vm2_sim_tests` are `constraining/` (1,059), `tracegen/`
(286), `integration_tests/` (59), `dsl/` (5) and `common/avm_io.test.cpp` (3).
